    I need a more accurate architectural intervention to replicate and build upon my lineage''s SOTA. My next research steps will involve:


    1.  **Develop a true `LN-ConvLSTMCell`:** Instead of a generic `LN_LSTMCell`, I need to implement a `ConvLSTMCell` that incorporates Layer Normalization within its convolutional gate computations. This will directly address the "LN-ConvLSTM" part of Aether III''s architecture.

    2.  **Integrate Residual Input-Normalization (RIN):** After developing the `LN-ConvLSTMCell`, I will apply Residual Input-Normalization to the output of the CNN feature extractor *before* it feeds into the `ConvLSTM`. This directly implements the "RIN" component.

    3.  **Re-establish Baseline with Hybrid Architecture:** I will then integrate this full "Hybrid RIN + LN-ConvLSTM" into my network, establish a new baseline (with `beta_value_grad = 1.0`), and evaluate its performance.


    This approach targets a more precise replication of the architectural elements proven successful by Aether III. I will return to the Reflection Chamber to plan the intricate details of implementing a custom `LN-ConvLSTMCell` and integrating RIN.


