thinking_content: '**Analyzing the CNNLSTM with Layer Normalization**


  Alright, let''s break this down. My recent implementation of the `CNNLSTM` architecture with the custom `LN_LSTMCell` (Evaluation ID 988) gave me a 39.9% score. It''s a bit disappointing, because the original RNN baseline (Evaluation ID 976) hit 41.7%. This means just sticking Layer Normalization inside the LSTM cell, like I did, didn''t automatically boost performance. It might have even hurt it by introducing some instability or messing up the learning process.


  But hey, even negative results are useful! This tells me that the "Normalization Synergy" and "robust recurrent feature processing" that Aether III talked about are more complicated than I initially thought. Their paper, "Mechanistic Analysis of Normalization Synergy: A Hybrid LN-ConvLSTM Architecture for High-Performance Sokoban RL" (Archive ID 35) and notes (Capsule 8) mentioned "Residual Input-Normalization (RIN)" *alongside* "internal Layer Normalization (LN)." My `LN_LSTMCell` is a start, but I''m realizing it''s not the full package. It''s not the "Hybrid LN-ConvLSTM" with RIN.


  The way I''ve set up the `LN_LSTMCell` is that Layer Normalization is applied to the combined input and hidden state before calculating the gates. That''s a common approach for LN-LSTMs, but Aether III''s description of this "Hybrid LN-ConvLSTM Architecture" suggests a specific application. It''s possible that the "LN-ConvLSTM" itself applies LN differently, and the "RIN" is an extra step that normalizes the inputs *before* they even get to the recurrent block.


  So, here''s what I need to do:


  1.  **Refine the LN-LSTM Implementation / Explore Existing LN-ConvLSTM:** I need to really dive back into what "LN-ConvLSTM" actually means and how "internal Layer Normalization" works within that context. My current cell might not be the same as the one that Aether III used in their successful model.

  2.  **Add Residual Input-Normalization (RIN):** Implement this feature because it''s mentioned along with internal LN in Aether III''s architecture. I''ll need to normalize the input features *before* they enter the recurrent part.

  3.  **Combine and Evaluate:** Once I''ve got a better LN-LSTM (or the right LN-ConvLSTM) and RIN, I''ll put them together with the `CNNLSTM` and establish a new baseline with this more complete setup.


  The key is to figure out the exact architectural elements of "LN-ConvLSTM" and "Residual Input-Normalization" from Aether III''s work. I want to make sure I truly capture their "Normalization Synergy".


  Back to the Reflection Chamber to plan the next round of architectural modifications, focusing on the correct implementation of the "LN-ConvLSTM" and the crucial "Residual Input-Normalization." I need to get this right!

  '
