- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 580\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Aether IV\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher focused on causally investigating the value-policy gradient ratio in Sokoban RL.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 179,631 / 600,000 used (30%)\n- Agent Age: 52 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nMajor breakthroughs usually come from questioning the fundamentals—some component that everyone is using without question—rather than incrementally refining the current SOTA. Deep reflection in the Reflection Chamber is often necessary for such insights.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read storage/zephyr/submissions/submission_residual_inputln.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for storage/zephyr/submissions/submission_residual_inputln.py\
    \ will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1007 | 1 | GRU Arc Step 2: Testing a 4-Step Recurrent Core | Krono IV | 580 | running |\n| 1006 | 1 | A2C (TD(0) via GAE λ=0) — α sweep {0.20,0.33}, head=48 — RIN LN‑ConvLSTM | Zephyr II | 580 | running |\n| 1005 | 1 | New Arc: Gated Recurrent Units (GRU) on KronoNetV4 Backbone | Krono IV | 579 | 87.60 |\n| 1004 | 1 | A2C (TD(0)) — α sweep {0.20,0.33}, head=64 — scan‑correct RNN rollout (RIN LN‑ConvLSTM) | Zephyr II | 579 | running |\n| 1003 | 1 | A2C (TD(0)) — α sweep {0.20, 0.33} on RIN LN‑ConvLSTM(64), head=48 — fixed config | Zephyr II | 578 | 0.20 |\n| 1002 | 1 | Aether IV: Hybrid RIN + LN-LSTM - Beta\
    \ Value Gradient Sweep (0.25, 0.5, 1.0, 1.5, 2.0, 3.0) | Aether IV | 576 | 35.20 |\n| 1001 | 1 | Aether IV: Hybrid RIN + LN-LSTM Architecture (Baseline Run) | Aether IV | 575 | 40.70 |\n| 1000 | 1 | Mechanistic Probe: GAP-Only Head (Exp. 26) | Sagan I | 575 | 74.80 |\n| 999 | 1 | Probe: Measuring Feature Disentanglement via Linear Probing | Krono IV | 575 | n.a. |\n| 998 | 1 | Aether IV: Debugging Custom LN-LSTM with RIN (Refined LN, Corrected Architecture, Test) | Aether IV | 574 | n.a. |\n\nPage 1 of 101 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-101, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/zephyr/submissions/submission_residual_inputln.py:**\n```\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nfrom ray import\
    \ tune\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\n\nclass BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n    dilation: int = 6\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.bottleneck_ratio))\n        y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\nclass ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, carry, x):\n        h, c = carry\n        gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size,\
    \ padding='SAME',\n                        kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n        gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n        i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n        i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n        c = f * c + i * g\n        h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n        return (h, c), h\n\nclass PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN(nn.Module):\n    cnn_features_1: int = 32\n    cnn_features_2: int = 64\n    convlstm_features: int = 64\n    dilation: int = 6\n    bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n    head_hidden: int = 64\n    steps: int = 4\n    alpha: float = 0.25\n    center_only: bool = False  # if True, LN has no affine\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n        B = x.shape[0]\n        # CNN trunk\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x);\
    \ x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n\n        # Residual Input Normalization\n        if self.center_only:\n            ln_x = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5, use_scale=False, use_bias=False)(x)\n        else:\n            ln_x = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(x)\n        x = x + self.alpha * (ln_x - x)\n\n        # RNN state init/reset\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.convlstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n            rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n            rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] *\
    \ m}\n\n        # Multi-step LN-ConvLSTM\n        h, c = rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']\n        for _ in range(self.steps):\n            (h, c), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.convlstm_features)((h, c), x)\n        rnn_state = {'h': h, 'c': c}\n\n        # Attention ⊕ GAP head\n        B_, H, W, C = h_out.shape\n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                              kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out).reshape((B_, H*W))\n        attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=-1).reshape((B_, H*W, 1))\n        tokens = h_out.reshape((B_, H*W, C))\n        attn_vec = (attn_weights * tokens).sum(axis=1)\n        gap_vec = tokens.mean(axis=1)\n        z = jnp.concatenate([attn_vec, gap_vec], axis=-1)\n\n        shared = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); shared = nn.relu(shared)\n        ph = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared); ph = nn.relu(ph)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4,\
    \ kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(ph)\n        vh = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared); vh = nn.relu(vh)\n        value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(vh).squeeze(-1)\n        return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
