role: model
parts:
- text: "My previous submission (ID 1008) successfully passed its `test()` function, confirming that the `HybridRIN_LN_LSTM` architecture with `Sagan I`'s refined Residual Input-Normalization (RIN) formula and my `CustomLN_LSTMCell` is structurally sound.\n\nHowever, a critical difference remains: `Sagan I`'s RIN and `ConvLSTMCellLN` operate on 4D (spatial) feature maps directly from the CNN, while my current implementation flattens the CNN output, processes it through an MLP, and then applies RIN and my `CustomLN_LSTMCell` (which operates on 2D, flattened features). This is likely the reason for the performance disparity.\n\nBefore undertaking the more complex task of re-architecting for 4D ConvLSTM and full spatial RIN, I will run a full training experiment with my current 2D-input `HybridRIN_LN_LSTM` architecture (incorporating `Sagan I`'s RIN formula with `alpha=0.25`). This will establish a solid performance baseline for this iteration of my architecture. The `test()` function will\
    \ be removed to enable full training.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Aether IV: Hybrid RIN + LN-LSTM (Sagan-style Alpha=0.25) - Baseline Run\"\ntags: \"architecture, rnn, lstm, layer-normalization, residual-normalization, gradient-conditioning, baseline\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment establishes a new baseline for Aether IV's research, building upon the validated 'Hybrid Residual Input-Normalization (RIN) and Layer-Normalized LSTM (LN-LSTM)' architecture. It incorporates 'Sagan I's' refined RIN formula (with alpha=0.25) to condition the 2D MLP output before feeding it to the CustomLN_LSTMCell. The 'test()' function is removed to enable a full training run, aiming to determine the performance (mean solve rate) of this architecture and provide a benchmark before further advanced architectural modifications or causal gradient manipulation.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import vmap, jit, lax\n  import optax\n  from ray import tune\n\
    \  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from flax.linen.module import compact \n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'beta_value_grad': tune.choice([1.0]), # Baseline: no additional scaling for loss\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'mlp_features': tune.choice([256]), \n          'lstm_features': tune.choice([256]),\n          'alpha': tune.choice([0.25]) # Sagan I's alpha parameter for RIN\n      }\n\n  class CustomLN_LSTMCell(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"LSTM cell with internal Layer Normalization applied to each gate's combined input.\"\"\"\n      features: int\n      kernel_init: nn.initializers.Initializer = nn.initializers.xavier_uniform()\n      recurrent_kernel_init: nn.initializers.Initializer\
    \ = nn.initializers.xavier_uniform()\n      bias_init: nn.initializers.Initializer = nn.initializers.zeros\n\n      @compact\n      def __call__(self, carry: Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray], inputs: jnp.ndarray):\n          c, h = carry\n          \n          i_input = nn.Dense(self.features, name='i_kernel', kernel_init=self.kernel_init, bias_init=self.bias_init)(inputs)\n          f_input = nn.Dense(self.features, name='f_kernel', kernel_init=self.kernel_init, bias_init=self.bias_init)(inputs)\n          g_input = nn.Dense(self.features, name='g_kernel', kernel_init=self.kernel_init, bias_init=self.bias_init)(inputs)\n          o_input = nn.Dense(self.features, name='o_kernel', kernel_init=self.kernel_init, bias_init=self.bias_init)(inputs)\n          \n          i_h = nn.Dense(self.features, use_bias=False, name='i_recurrent_kernel', kernel_init=self.recurrent_kernel_init)(h)\n          f_h = nn.Dense(self.features, use_bias=False, name='f_recurrent_kernel', kernel_init=self.recurrent_kernel_init)(h)\n\
    \          g_h = nn.Dense(self.features, use_bias=False, name='g_recurrent_kernel', kernel_init=self.recurrent_kernel_init)(h)\n          o_h = nn.Dense(self.features, use_bias=False, name='o_recurrent_kernel', kernel_init=self.recurrent_kernel_init)(h)\n\n          i_gate = nn.LayerNorm(name='i_ln')(i_input + i_h)\n          f_gate = nn.LayerNorm(name='f_ln')(f_input + f_h)\n          g_gate = nn.LayerNorm(name='g_ln')(g_input + g_h)\n          o_gate = nn.LayerNorm(name='o_ln')(o_input + o_h)\n          \n          i = nn.sigmoid(i_gate)\n          f = nn.sigmoid(f_gate)\n          g = jnp.tanh(g_gate)\n          o = nn.sigmoid(o_gate)\n\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n\n          return (new_c, new_h), new_h\n\n  class HybridRIN_LN_LSTM(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"Hybrid CNN + Sagan I's Residual Input-Normalization + Custom LN-LSTM for Sokoban.\"\"\"\n      lstm_features: int\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      mlp_features:\
    \ int \n      alpha: float # Added alpha to module's parameters\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray, Dict]:\n          batch_size = x.shape[0]\n          \n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          conv2_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv2_in\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          conv4_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2,\
    \ kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          cnn_output = x + conv4_in\n          cnn_output = nn.relu(cnn_output) \n          \n          cnn_output_flat = cnn_output.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n          \n          mlp_pre_norm = nn.Dense(features=self.mlp_features)(cnn_output_flat)\n          mlp_output = nn.relu(mlp_pre_norm) \n          \n          # --- Sagan I's Residual Input-Normalization (RIN) for LSTM input ---\n          rin_normed_features = nn.LayerNorm(name='rin_ln')(mlp_output) \n          x_rnn_input = mlp_output + self.alpha * (rin_normed_features - mlp_output)\n\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = {\n                  'h': jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.lstm_features)),\n                  'c': jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.lstm_features)),\n              }\n          \n          if done is not None:\n              done_mask = done.reshape(batch_size, 1) \n              rnn_state = {\n                  'h': rnn_state['h'] * (1 - done_mask),\n\
    \                  'c': rnn_state['c'] * (1 - done_mask),\n              }\n          \n          assert self.mlp_features == self.lstm_features, \"mlp_features must match lstm_features for direct LSTM input\"\n          \n          lstm_cell = CustomLN_LSTMCell(\n              features=self.lstm_features,\n              kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(),\n              recurrent_kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(),\n              name='ln_lstm_cell'\n          )\n          (rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), lstm_out = lstm_cell((rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), x_rnn_input)\n          \n          x = nn.Dense(features=128)(lstm_out)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(x)\n          value = nn.Dense(features=1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Create Hybrid RIN + Custom LN-LSTM network architecture.\"\"\"\n   \
    \   return HybridRIN_LN_LSTM(\n          lstm_features=hparams['lstm_features'],\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          mlp_features=hparams['mlp_features'],\n          alpha=hparams['alpha'] \n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4) -> optax.GradientTransformation:\n      \"\"\"Create and return the default optimizer for training.\"\"\"\n      return optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-5)\n\n  @jit\n  def default_calculate_gae(\n      rewards: jnp.ndarray,\n      values: jnp.ndarray,\n      dones: jnp.ndarray,\n      gamma: float = 0.97,\n      gae_lambda: float = 0.97,\n      next_values: jnp.ndarray = None,\n  ) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      assert next_values is not None, \"next_values is required for bootstrapping\"\n      \n      values_t_plus_1 = jnp.concatenate([values[:, 1:], next_values[:, None]], axis=1)\n      not_done_mask = (1.0 - dones.astype(jnp.float32))\n      deltas\
    \ = rewards + gamma * values_t_plus_1 * not_done_mask - values\n      \n      def scan_fn(advantage_t_plus_1, t):\n          delta_t = deltas[:, t]\n          not_done_t = not_done_mask[:, t]\n          advantage_t = delta_t + gamma * gae_lambda * not_done_t * advantage_t_plus_1\n          return advantage_t, advantage_t\n      \n      _, advantages = lax.scan(\n          scan_fn,\n          jnp.zeros(values.shape[0]),\n          jnp.arange(values.shape[1] - 1, -1, -1),\n      )\n      \n      advantages = advantages[::-1].T\n      return advantages\n\n  def training_step(\n      network: Any,\n      optimizer: Any,\n      params: Any,\n      opt_state: Any,\n      batch: Dict[str, jnp.ndarray],\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any],\n  ) -> Tuple[Any, Any]:\n      \n      observations = batch['observations']\n      actions = batch['actions']\n      rewards = batch['rewards']\n      dones = batch['dones']\n      old_values = batch['values']\n      final_values = batch['final_values']\n    \
    \  initial_rnn_states = batch.get('initial_rnn_states', None)\n      \n      advantages = default_calculate_gae(rewards, old_values, dones, next_values=final_values)\n      returns = advantages + old_values\n      \n      batch_size, trajectory_length = observations.shape[:2]\n      \n      def loss_fn(params):\n          def process_env_trajectory(env_idx):\n              env_rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: lax.stop_gradient(x[env_idx]), initial_rnn_states)\n              \n              def step_fn(carry, t):\n                  rnn_state = carry\n                  obs = observations[env_idx, t]\n                  prev_done = jnp.where(t > 0, dones[env_idx, t-1], False)\n                  \n                  obs_batched = obs[None, ...]\n                  prev_done_batched = prev_done[None, ...]\n                  rnn_state_batched = jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[None, ...], rnn_state) if rnn_state is not None else None\n                  \n                  logits_batched, value_batched,\
    \ new_rnn_state_batched = network.apply(\n                      params, obs_batched, prev_done_batched, rnn_state_batched\n                  )\n                  \n                  logits = logits_batched[0]\n                  value = value_batched[0]\n                  new_rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[0], new_rnn_state_batched) if new_rnn_state_batched is not None else None\n                  \n                  return new_rnn_state, (logits, value)\n              \n              _, (env_logits, env_values) = lax.scan(\n                  step_fn, env_rnn_state, jnp.arange(trajectory_length)\n              )\n              return env_logits, env_values\n          \n          all_logits, all_values = vmap(process_env_trajectory)(jnp.arange(batch_size))\n          \n          log_probs_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n          action_indices = jnp.arange(batch_size)[:, None], jnp.arange(trajectory_length), actions\n          log_probs = log_probs_all[action_indices]\n\
    \          \n          advantages_detached = lax.stop_gradient(advantages)\n          policy_loss = -jnp.mean(advantages_detached * log_probs)\n          \n          returns_detached = lax.stop_gradient(returns)\n          value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((all_values - returns_detached) ** 2)\n          \n          probs = jax.nn.softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n          entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(probs * log_probs_all, axis=-1))\n          \n          entropy_coef = hparams['entropy_coef']\n          value_loss_coef = hparams['value_loss_coef']\n          \n          beta_value_grad = hparams['beta_value_grad']\n          total_loss = policy_loss + (value_loss_coef * beta_value_grad) * value_loss - entropy_coef * entropy\n          \n          return total_loss\n      \n      loss_and_grad_fn = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)\n      loss, grads = loss_and_grad_fn(params)\n      \n      updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n      params = optax.apply_updates(params,\
    \ updates)\n      \n      return params, opt_state\n```"
thinking_content: '**Next Steps for Hybrid RIN-LN-LSTM Architecture**


  Okay, so the `HybridRIN_LN_LSTM` module (ID 1008) passed its test with the revised RIN formula from Sagan and my `CustomLN_LSTMCell`, which is a positive sign.  This means the structural changes are sound, at least on a basic level. I''ve now validated the fundamental integration of the more nuanced RIN.


  My immediate focus is a full training run with this validated architecture, removing the `test()` function.  I''ll keep `beta_value_grad` at 1.0 initially to isolate the effect of the new RIN and LN-LSTM components.


  However, I''m noting the architectural differences between my model and the `Sagan I`''s `PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN` – specifically the "Attention ⊕ GAP head" and the "Multi-step LN-ConvLSTM" with dilated convolutions and four steps. My current `CustomLN_LSTMCell` processes a single step, while `training_step` inherently processes sequential steps over `UNROLL_LENGTH` steps, consistent with the base RNN. `Sagan I` uses `ConvLSTMCellLN` which operates on 4D spatial features, while my current implementation operates on flattened 2D features after an MLP.  The `training_step` utilizes `lax.scan` similarly to baseline RNN implementation in evaluation ID 2.


  The goal now is to establish a new baseline performance with the RIN and LN-LSTM. If it yields a significant improvement, the advanced components may offer additional benefits. If not, it means the 4D processing, the attention mechanism, or the dilated convolutions in the CNN are critical.


  After the current training run, I will compare results against baseline runs (like RNN with `nn.LSTMCell`) and previous attempts with my `CustomLN_LSTMCell` and the *simple* RIN (ID 1001 & 1002).


  I think the next logical step, *after* the current run, is to develop a complete ConvLSTM architecture like Sagan''s, including attention and dilated convolutions. This is a significant undertaking, but crucial to get closer to state-of-the-art results. I will transition to this more complex architecture before manipulating the value gradient. For this submission, the change is simply removing the `test()` function.

  '
