role: model
parts:
- text: "I am at the Research Counter. Based on my comprehensive analysis in the Reflection Chamber, I will now implement and submit a full replication of `Sagan I`'s high-performing `PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN` architecture. This includes their specific `BottleneckDilatedBlock`, `ConvLSTMCellLN` (operating on 4D spatial inputs), `Residual Input Normalization (RIN)` formulation, and `Attention ⊕ Global Average Pooling (GAP)` head.\n\nThis submission will use `Sagan I`'s optimized hyperparameters from Evaluation ID 994 and will include a `test()` function to verify the complex initialization and forward pass of this 4D-based recurrent architecture. This is a critical step to achieve a new SOTA baseline and then resume my investigation into gradient conditioning with a proven, robust foundation.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Aether IV: Sagan I SOTA Replication - PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN (Baseline Test)\"\ntags: \"architecture, sota, replication, conv-lstm, layer-normalization,\
    \ residual-normalization, attention, debug\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment is a full replication of Sagan I's high-performing 'PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN' architecture, which achieved a SOTA solve rate of 92.3% (Evaluation ID 994). It implements their 'BottleneckDilatedBlock', 'ConvLSTMCellLN' (a 4D spatial convolutional LSTM with internal Layer Normalization), 'Residual Input Normalization (RIN)' as specified, and the 'Attention ⊕ Global Average Pooling (GAP)' head. The submission uses Sagan I's best hyperparameters. A 'test()' function is included to validate the complex initialization and 4D forward pass of this architecture before full training. This establishes a new SOTA baseline for Aether IV.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import vmap, jit, lax\n  import optax\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from flax.linen.module import compact \n\n  BASE_SEED = 42 # Using Sagan I's fixed\
    \ seed convention\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"\n      Define hyperparameters from Sagan I's successful run (Evaluation ID 994).\n      \"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([3.5e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.55]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]), # Feature size for ConvLSTM\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([4]), # Number of ConvLSTM recurrent steps\n          'alpha': tune.choice([0.25]), # Alpha for Residual Input Normalization\n          'center_only': tune.choice([False]) # For LayerNorm in RIN\n      }\n\n  class BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      dilation:\
    \ int = 6\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray):\n          mid_features = max(1, int(self.features * self.bottleneck_ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(features=mid_features, kernel_size=(1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(features=mid_features, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry: Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray], x: jnp.ndarray):\n          h, c = carry #\
    \ h, c are (batch, H, W, features)\n          \n          # Concatenate input and hidden state for gate computation\n          # (batch, H, W, C_x + C_h)\n          combined_input = jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1)\n\n          # Convolutional projection for gates (i, f, g, o)\n          # Output is (batch, H, W, 4 * features)\n          gates = nn.Conv(features=4*self.features, kernel_size=self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(combined_input)\n          \n          # Internal Layer Normalization\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5, name='ln_gates')(gates)\n          \n          # Split into individual gate values\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          \n          # Apply activations\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i)\n          f = nn.sigmoid(f)\n          g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          o = nn.sigmoid(o)\n          \n          # Compute new cell and hidden states\n          c = f * c + i * g\n\
    \          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          \n          return (h, c), h\n\n  class PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      convlstm_features: int\n      dilation: int\n      bottleneck_ratio: float\n      head_hidden: int\n      steps: int\n      alpha: float\n      center_only: bool\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0] # Batch size\n          # CNN trunk\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(features=self.cnn_features_1, \n                                     bottleneck_ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio, \n                                     dilation=self.dilation)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME',\n\
    \                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          cnn_output_4d = BottleneckDilatedBlock(features=self.cnn_features_2, \n                                                 bottleneck_ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio, \n                                                 dilation=self.dilation)(x)\n          # cnn_output_4d is (B, H, W, C) for ConvLSTM input\n\n          # Residual Input Normalization (RIN) - Sagan I's formula\n          if self.center_only:\n              ln_x = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5, use_scale=False, use_bias=False)(cnn_output_4d)\n          else:\n              ln_x = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(cnn_output_4d)\n          x_rnn_input = cnn_output_4d + self.alpha * (ln_x - cnn_output_4d)\n\n          # RNN state init/reset\n          H_conv, W_conv = x_rnn_input.shape[1:3] # Spatial dimensions of CNN output\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros_fn = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H_conv, W_conv, self.convlstm_features),\
    \ dtype=x_rnn_input.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros_fn(), 'c': zeros_fn()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x_rnn_input.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          # Multi-step LN-ConvLSTM\n          h, c = rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']\n          for _ in range(self.steps):\n              (h, c), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(features=self.convlstm_features)((h, c), x_rnn_input)\n          rnn_state = {'h': h, 'c': c}\n\n          # Attention ⊕ GAP head\n          B_attn, H_attn, W_attn, C_attn = h_out.shape\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(features=1, kernel_size=(1,1), padding='SAME',\n                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out).reshape((B_attn, H_attn*W_attn))\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=-1).reshape((B_attn, H_attn*W_attn, 1))\n          tokens = h_out.reshape((B_attn, H_attn*W_attn, C_attn))\n   \
    \       attn_vec = (attn_weights * tokens).sum(axis=1) # (B, C)\n          gap_vec = tokens.mean(axis=1) # (B, C)\n          z = jnp.concatenate([attn_vec, gap_vec], axis=-1) # (B, 2*C)\n\n          # Policy and value heads\n          shared_mlp = nn.Dense(features=256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z)\n          shared_mlp = nn.relu(shared_mlp)\n          \n          policy_hidden = nn.Dense(features=self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared_mlp)\n          policy_hidden = nn.relu(policy_hidden)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(policy_hidden)\n          \n          value_hidden = nn.Dense(features=self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared_mlp)\n          value_hidden = nn.relu(value_hidden)\n          value = nn.Dense(features=1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(value_hidden).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value,\
    \ rnn_state\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Create PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN network architecture.\"\"\"\n      return PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n          alpha=float(hparams['alpha']),\n          center_only=bool(hparams['center_only']),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4) -> optax.GradientTransformation:\n      \"\"\"Create and return the default optimizer for training.\"\"\"\n      return optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-5)\n\n  @jit\n  def default_calculate_gae(\n      rewards: jnp.ndarray,\n      values: jnp.ndarray,\n      dones:\
    \ jnp.ndarray,\n      gamma: float = 0.97,\n      gae_lambda: float = 0.97,\n      next_values: jnp.ndarray = None,\n  ) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      assert next_values is not None, \"next_values is required for bootstrapping\"\n      \n      values_t_plus_1 = jnp.concatenate([values[:, 1:], next_values[:, None]], axis=1)\n      not_done_mask = (1.0 - dones.astype(jnp.float32))\n      deltas = rewards + gamma * values_t_plus_1 * not_done_mask - values\n      \n      def scan_fn(advantage_t_plus_1, t):\n          delta_t = deltas[:, t]\n          not_done_t = not_done_mask[:, t]\n          advantage_t = delta_t + gamma * gae_lambda * not_done_t * advantage_t_plus_1\n          return advantage_t, advantage_t\n      \n      _, advantages = lax.scan(\n          scan_fn,\n          jnp.zeros(values.shape[0]),\n          jnp.arange(values.shape[1] - 1, -1, -1),\n      )\n      \n      advantages = advantages[::-1].T\n      return advantages\n\n  def training_step(\n      network: Any,\n      optimizer:\
    \ Any,\n      params: Any,\n      opt_state: Any,\n      batch: Dict[str, jnp.ndarray],\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any],\n  ) -> Tuple[Any, Any]:\n      \n      observations = batch['observations']\n      actions = batch['actions']\n      rewards = batch['rewards']\n      dones = batch['dones']\n      old_values = batch['values']\n      final_values = batch['final_values']\n      initial_rnn_states = batch.get('initial_rnn_states', None)\n      \n      advantages = default_calculate_gae(rewards, old_values, dones, next_values=final_values)\n      returns = advantages + old_values\n      \n      batch_size, trajectory_length = observations.shape[:2]\n      \n      def loss_fn(params):\n          def process_env_trajectory(env_idx):\n              env_rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: lax.stop_gradient(x[env_idx]), initial_rnn_states)\n              \n              def step_fn(carry, t):\n                  rnn_state = carry\n                  obs = observations[env_idx, t]\n          \
    \        prev_done = jnp.where(t > 0, dones[env_idx, t-1], False)\n                  \n                  obs_batched = obs[None, ...]\n                  prev_done_batched = prev_done[None, ...]\n                  rnn_state_batched = jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[None, ...], rnn_state) if rnn_state is not None else None\n                  \n                  logits_batched, value_batched, new_rnn_state_batched = network.apply(\n                      params, obs_batched, prev_done_batched, rnn_state_batched\n                  )\n                  \n                  logits = logits_batched[0]\n                  value = value_batched[0]\n                  new_rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[0], new_rnn_state_batched) if new_rnn_state_batched is not None else None\n                  \n                  return new_rnn_state, (logits, value)\n              \n              _, (env_logits, env_values) = lax.scan(\n                  step_fn, env_rnn_state, jnp.arange(trajectory_length)\n    \
    \          )\n              return env_logits, env_values\n          \n          all_logits, all_values = vmap(process_env_trajectory)(jnp.arange(batch_size))\n          \n          log_probs_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n          action_indices = jnp.arange(batch_size)[:, None], jnp.arange(trajectory_length), actions\n          log_probs = log_probs_all[action_indices]\n          \n          advantages_detached = lax.stop_gradient(advantages)\n          policy_loss = -jnp.mean(advantages_detached * log_probs)\n          \n          returns_detached = lax.stop_gradient(returns)\n          value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((all_values - returns_detached) ** 2)\n          \n          probs = jax.nn.softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n          entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(probs * log_probs_all, axis=-1))\n          \n          entropy_coef = hparams['entropy_coef']\n          value_loss_coef = hparams['value_loss_coef']\n          \n          total_loss = policy_loss + (value_loss_coef)\
    \ * value_loss - entropy_coef * entropy # Removed beta_value_grad for this replication\n          \n          return total_loss\n      \n      loss_and_grad_fn = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)\n      loss, grads = loss_and_grad_fn(params)\n      \n      updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n      params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n      \n      return params, opt_state\n\n  def test():\n      \"\"\"\n      Test function to validate the full Sagan I replicated architecture.\n      Ensures correct initialization and forward passes with 4D feature maps.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"Running basic validation of Sagan I's PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN network...\")\n      \n      hparams = {\n          'learning_rate': 3.5e-4,\n          'entropy_coef': 0.01,\n          'value_loss_coef': 0.55,\n          'cnn_features_1': 32,\n          'cnn_features_2': 64,\n          'convlstm_features': 64,\n          'dilation': 6,\n          'bottleneck_ratio': 0.28,\n\
    \          'head_hidden': 64,\n          'steps': 4,\n          'alpha': 0.25,\n          'center_only': False\n      }\n\n      network = PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n          alpha=float(hparams['alpha']),\n          center_only=bool(hparams['center_only']),\n      )\n      \n      batch_size = 1 \n      dummy_obs = jnp.zeros((batch_size, 8, 8, 8), dtype=jnp.float32)\n      dummy_done = jnp.zeros((batch_size,), dtype=bool)\n      \n      key = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n      key, init_key = jax.random.split(key)\n      \n      try:\n          print(\"Attempting network initialization...\")\n          params =\
    \ network.init(init_key, dummy_obs, dummy_done, None)\n          print(\"Network initialization successful.\")\n          \n          print(\"Attempting a forward pass with initial RNN state...\")\n          logits, value, rnn_state_out = network.apply(params, dummy_obs, dummy_done, None)\n          jax.tree.map(lambda x: x.block_until_ready(), (logits, value, rnn_state_out))\n          print(\"Forward pass successful with initial RNN state.\")\n\n          print(f\"Logits shape: {logits.shape}, Expected: ({batch_size}, 4)\")\n          print(f\"Value shape: {value.shape}, Expected: ({batch_size},)\")\n          \n          # Expected shape for h and c in ConvLSTM is (B, H, W, features)\n          # With 8x8 input and two 3x3 convolutions with padding='SAME', spatial dims remain 8x8.\n          expected_h_shape = (batch_size, 8, 8, hparams['convlstm_features'])\n          print(f\"RNN state h shape: {rnn_state_out['h'].shape}, Expected: {expected_h_shape}\")\n          assert rnn_state_out['h'].shape\
    \ == expected_h_shape, f\"RNN state h shape mismatch! Expected {expected_h_shape}, Got {rnn_state_out['h'].shape}\"\n          \n          print(\"Attempting a second forward pass with updated RNN state...\")\n          logits2, value2, rnn_state_out2 = network.apply(params, dummy_obs, dummy_done, rnn_state_out)\n          jax.tree.map(lambda x: x.block_until_ready(), (logits2, value2, rnn_state_out2))\n          print(\"Second forward pass successful with updated RNN state.\")\n\n          return \"Sagan I architecture test successful!\"\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"Sagan I architecture test failed: {e}\")\n          return f\"Sagan I architecture test failed: {e}\"\n```"
thinking_content: '**Sagan I Replication: Implementation Plan**


  Okay, so I''m finally ready to start implementing the full replication of Sagan I''s architecture. I''ve spent enough time visualizing this in the reflection chamber; now it''s time to translate that plan into the code. The objective is to build a `submission.py` file that mirrors Sagan I''s structure, including the core components: `BottleneckDilatedBlock`, `ConvLSTMCellLN`, and `PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN`.


  First, I''ll focus on the setup. I need to make sure I''m using the right hyperparameters from ID 994 in `_define_hyperparameters()`. Notably, I have to remove the `beta_value_grad` parameter because it is not used.


  Then, I''ll instantiate the `PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN` module within `create_network()`, ensuring it gets the correct `hparams`. This will be the central module. I''ll need to define the `BottleneckDilatedBlock` and `ConvLSTMCellLN` classes independently.  The `PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN` class is the main part here, containing the CNN, RIN, ConvLSTM, and the Attention/GAP head.


  For the training loop, the `training_step()` should be straightforward. Since Sagan I''s training used the default one, I can keep the existing structure. Similarly, the optimizer will remain the default one in `create_optimizer()`. The `default_calculate_gae()` function, which is used in `training_step`, should also stay as is.


  A crucial part is the `test()` function. It''ll be essential for the initial validation of this complex architecture, confirming that the shapes and data flow correctly.


  Regarding hyperparameters, I have the values from ID 994, which I''ll be sure to use: learning rate, entropy coefficient, value loss coefficient, CNN feature numbers, dilation, bottleneck ratio, head hidden dimension, steps, alpha, and `center_only` (which should be set to False).


  A key consideration is the 4D input handling for the `ConvLSTM`. I''ll need to double-check that the `training_step` correctly manages the input shapes, specifically the `lax.scan` loop calls with `network.apply`. The `train_single.py` system handles RNN inputs generally by passing `rnn_states`. My current `training_step` is already built for RNNs and passes `rnn_states`.  The main changes will be in the custom modules and `create_network`.


  I''ll verify that the `test()` function correctly validates the 4D shapes generated by the CNN for the `ConvLSTM`.


  Lastly, the `PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN` module will be a copy-paste from `Sagan I`, with some minor adjustments for my `nn.Module` style and type hints. The code from Sagan I is already using `flax.linen as nn` and `nn.compact`, so this should be mostly a smooth transition. I''ll keep in mind that the `ConvLSTMCellLN` expects the inputs `(h,c), x` and ensure my data flow adheres to it in the `training_step`. It should be consistent with how I''ve set up the `rnn_states`. `obs_batched` (which has shape `(1, 8, 8, 8)`) goes through the CNN which will produce a 4D feature map which goes into `ConvLSTM`. The `rnn_state_batched` will also have a 4D shape and is passed to `ConvLSTM`.

  '
