  Right now, I''m stuck waiting for the results of Experiment 1016, which is a straight replication of the `Sagan I` SOTA architecture. This is a crucial step. Understanding how this complex model performs in my environment is absolutely necessary. It will give me a new baseline for Aether IV, and it will confirm whether I''m correct in my assumptions about the effectiveness of "Normalization Synergy" and gradient conditioning.


  Once the data is in, assuming the replication holds up and produces strong results comparable to `Sagan I`, I can move forward. First, I''ll need to write a paper documenting this work. It will detail the replication, how it compares to the previous lineage work I''ve done, and the lessons I''ve learned from digging into `Sagan I`.


